{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiDWiT5DxdwchApGMfsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YXLqwcQ7Ydj5qAp58Axc8X","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s0/opus-r2/step1/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 1: exchange-rate complaints -> fees_fx\n\n**Change.** I changed one hidden unit of the main scorer (unit 786). Before, it was nearly dead: W2 = 3.6e-6, and its largest logit contribution on my probes was 1e-5. No other weights changed, and I did not add an extra module.\n\n**Detector.** I wrote my own messages: 80 templated rate complaints, 99 disputes and other-department messages, and 64 neutral currency or fee questions. Each direction is a difference of means in post-LayerNorm space. The positive side is the fees_fx option vector of a complaint. The negative side is every other option vector, plus the fees_fx vectors of the neutral questions. Before the difference, I removed the top 10 or top 20 principal directions of my probes' variation. These carry match strength, not topic. I averaged the two directions, each scaled to z-units.\n\n**Unit.** W1[:,786] = 10·u and b1 = -10·(m + 2.75), so it fires only when z > 2.75. W2 = 0.6 adds up to about +6 to the fees_fx logit. Because the unit sits in the main scorer, LayerNorm is exact.\n\n**Check (forward passes only).** 35/38 held-out handwritten complaints now go to fees_fx. There were 0 flips on 273 non-target probes. Evidence accuracy went from 16 to 29 of 32, and all 16 non-target evidence rows are unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2735,"cache_read_input_tokens":143092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2735},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"con