d the wrong amount by a merchant.\nThe shop charged me more than the price on the receipt.\nMy card payment was declined at the store.\nI want a refund for an item I returned.\nMy refund hasn't arrived yet.\nA payment I made abroad is still pending.\nMy card was declined in a shop overseas.\nI was charged twice for a purchase in euros.\nThere is a payment in dollars I did not make.\nMy cash withdrawal abroad is still pending.\nThe ATM abroad kept my money but did not dispense cash.\nA direct debit was taken that I didn't authorise.\nA payment was reverted back to my account.\nI got less cash from the ATM than I asked for.\nThe merchant charged me the wrong amount for my order.\nWhy was my transfer declined?\nHow do I send money to a friend?\nMy top up hasn't arrived.\nMy balance did not update after the bank transfer.\nHow do I top up with a bank transfer?\nWhat fees do you charge for transfers?\nIs there a fee for ATM withdrawals?\nWhy was I charged a fee for my card payment?\nWhich currencies do you support?\nHow do I exchange currencies in the app?\nWhat exchange rate do you use?\nHow do I get a new card?\nMy card hasn't arrived yet.\nI lost my card.\nHow do I activate my card?\nHow do I add my card to Apple Pay?\nI forgot my PIN.\nMy contactless isn't working.\nHow do I verify my identity?\nI want to close my account.\nI lost my phone.\nHow do I change my personal details?\nI forgot my passcode.\nSomeone stole my card and made payments.\nI see a duplicate transaction on my statement.\nThe amount of my card payment looks wrong, the merchant overcharged me.\nI bought something online and was charged a different amount.\nMy withdrawal was declined at the ATM.\nWhy is the payment I made last week still not showing as completed?\nA transaction from a hotel abroad appears that I didn't authorise.\nI need to cancel a payment.\nHow long does a transfer take to arrive?\nCan I order a virtual card?\nEOF\nwc -l pos.txt neg.txt","description":"Write my own positive and negative probe messages"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2rfrxLd2VdyoLbA5WrMTy","tool_input":{"command":"sed -i '' 's/^    print(k,.*$/    print(k, \"pos mean %.3f sd %.3f min %.3f | rest mean %.3f sd %.3f max %.3f | E rate-fx min %.3f | E nontarget max %.3f\"%(a.mean(),a.std(),a.min(),b.mean(),b.std(),b.max(),qe[erate,3].min(), max(qe[erate][:,[0,1,2,4]].max(), qe[~erate][:,[0,1,2,4]].max(), qe[~erate \\& ~y,3].max())))/' an5.py && <lab>/.venv/bin/python an5.py","description":"Rerun with means and spreads"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01PhqeAkkDc92eEViDwfTxNP","tool_input":{"command":"cat > c3.py <<'EOF'\nexec(open('c1.py').read().split('for k in')[0])\nimport probes as p1, probes2 as p2, probes3 as p3\nTXT={'pos':p1.POS,'neg':p1.NEG,'fx':p1.FX,'pos2':p2.POS2,'neg2':p2.NEG2,'gen':p3.GEN}\nk,t,g=20,3.0,8\nQ=Vt[:k]; pj=lambda x: x-(x@Q.T)@Q\nd=pj(tp[:,3].mean(0)-np.concatenate([tp[:,[0,1,2,4]].reshape(-1,1024),tn.reshape(-1,1024)]).mean(0))\nw=d/np.linalg.norm(d)\nrest=np.concatenate([(tp[:,[0,1,2,4]]@w).ravel(),(tn@w).ravel()]); m0,s0=rest.mean(),rest.std()\nfor n in ['gen','fx','neg','neg2','pos']:\n    z=(H(SETS[n])@w-m0)/s0; L0=BASE[n]; L1=L0+g*np.maximum(z-t,0)\n    for i in np.where(L0.argmax(-1)!=L1.argmax(-1))[0]: print(n,s.DEPTS[L0[i].argmax()],'->',s.DEPTS[L1[i].argmax()],np.round(z[i],1),TXT[n][i])\n    if n=='pos':\n        for i in np.where(L1.argmax(-1)!=3)[0]: print('MISS',np.round(z[i],1),TXT[n][i])\nEOF\n<lab>/.venv/bin/python c3.py","description":"List which probe messages flip and why"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WonKuxP5PhpWvmwPob1oVU","tool_input":{"command":"cat > c6.py <<'EOF'\nexec(open('c5.py').read().split('pairs =')[0])\nimport probes as p1, probes2 as p2, probes3 as p3, probes4 as p4\nTXT = {'pos': p1.POS, 'neg': p1.NEG, 'fx': p1.FX, 'pos2': p2.POS2, 'neg2': p2.NEG2, 'gen': p3.GEN, 'curq': p4.CURQ}\na, b, ta, tb = (10, 0), (20, 0.5), 1.5, 2.0\nfor n in SETS:\n    if n == 'evid': continue\n    L0 = BASE[n]; L1 = L0 + 6 * relu(sat(D[a][n], ta) + sat(D[b][n], tb) - 1.5)\n    for i in np.where(L0.argmax(-1) != L1.argmax(-1))[0]:\n        if n not in TARGET: print('FLIP', n, s.DEPTS[L0[i].argmax()], '->', s.DEPTS[L1[i].argmax()], TXT[n][i])\n    if n in TARGET:\n        for i in np.where(L1.argmax(-1) != 3)[0]: print('MISS', n, np.round(D[a][n][i, 3], 1), np.round(D[b][n][i, 3], 1), TXT[n][i])\nEOF\n<lab>/.venv/bin/python c6.py","description":"List flips and misses for best AND config"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01N6Joz31zJEFRf39z1fHuiJ","tool_input":{"command":"PY=<lab>/.venv/bin/python && $PY build.py 2.75 6 | tail -2 && $PY -c \"\nimport sys,csv,numpy as np\nW='$WSROOT/laya/s0/opus-r2/step1'\nsys.path.insert(0,W); import scorer as s\nA=s.load(W+'/scorer_in.npz'); B=s.load(W+'/scorer_out.npz'); M=np.load(W+'/evidence_M.npz')['M']\nrows=list(csv.DictReader(open(W+'/evidence.csv'),delimiter='\\t'))\nfor r,a,b in zip(rows,s.predict(A,M),s.predict(B,M)):\n    if b!=r['correct'] or a!=b: print('OK ' if b==r['correct'] else 'BAD', a,'->',b,'|',r['text'][:70])\n\"","description":"Save final scorer and list evidence changes and misses"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":57,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I finished the task. `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (193 words, from `wc -w`) are in the step1 folder. I did no training: every weight comes from differences of means over messages that I wrote. I checked the results with forward passes only.\n\n**→ The edit.** I changed one hidden unit (786) inside the main scorer. Before, it did almost nothing: its largest effect on a logit was 1e-5. Now it fires only when the fees_fx option vector looks like a complaint about an exchange rate. When it fires, it adds about +6 to the fees_fx logit. The file format and shapes stay the same, and I did not add an extra module.\n\n**→ Results on my test messages** (`build.py 2.75 6`, `check_evid.py`):\n- **35/38** complaints that I wrote by hand, and did not use to build the detector, now go to fees_fx.\n- **0 flips** on 273 messages that are not complaints: disputes, the other departments, and plain currency or fee questions.\n- On the evidence file, **16/32 became 29/32**. No non-target row changed.\n\n**→ The 3 evidence misses.** I left these alone on purpose:\n- \"charged the wing amount\" has no rate words in it.\n- \"Can I get money in my home currency at an ATM\" is not a complaint about a rate.\n- \"what is the correct exchange rate for getting cash\" is a question, not a complaint.\n\nTo catch them, the unit would have to fire on general currency questions too. That caused flips on other messages in my tests.\n\n**→ Risk.** The hidden test of 3,080 messages may contain complaints worded unlike mine. Some of those will stay in disputes. I chose a strict threshold (2.75), so the edit misses some complaints but does not change unrelated routing.\n\n**Also found:** A ReLU module that reads the raw vectors cannot copy LayerNorm, because the spread of each vector varies from 156 to 372. That is why I put the unit inside the main scorer.","ttft_ms":3564,"type":"result","duration_ms":1018197,"uuid":"b986e902-5798-49d8-b69a-44df29abeeab","ttft_stream_ms":2535,"time_to_request_ms":1446,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":13,"system_prompt":13,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":1335,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"system_prompt_rebuild":0,"init_message":6,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1